\f1\fs22 \'91Excuse me dear, lady,\'92 an old, elongated man addressed Sarah, in what look like an elongated deep-purple child\'92s pyjama onesie festooned with an array of golden stars, ringed planets, and rainbows which appeared to issue from the armpits, groin and, yes, butthole.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah blinked, and hoped it would help shunt the gears of her gummed-up brain into overdrive. Her first feeling was one of relief. Even this guy and his two familiars standing behind were welcome changes from Johnny\'92s ranting. \'91Yes?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91May I present my card?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah took the small rectangle with two hands, exactly as the old man presented it with two. Who uses business cards any more? She read it:\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos Windus\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Principal Prophecy Facilitator\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Seven Sages Corp.\

\f3\i <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Don\'92t call us\'97heroes are called\'92
\f1\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah almost choked when she read the word, 
\f3\i heroes. 
\f1\i0 She glanced at Johnny, realising he was punking her, probably for dragging him into The Grotto for the second time in a month. \'91I think the person you\'92re looking for is my friend.\'92\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos, the wizard dude, tittered. \'91Oh, while all the world\'92s a stage, and we are all players, one Johnny Stoat is driving a shit-cart three blocks away.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What?\'92 Johnny protested, and adjusted his suit coat to emphasise how important he was.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>At the mention of Johnny\'92s name, Sarah hardened. \'91You put these derelicts up to this!\'92 she accused Johnny.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny\'92s mouth worked but issued only gargles of denial.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos looked crestfallen. \'91I assure you, our endeavours are sincere!\'92\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Uhuh,\'92 Sarah allowed. \'91So, what\'92s a \'85 
\f3\i Principal Prophecy Facilitator
\f1\i0 ?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Well you see, as worthy prophesies\'97and here I must assure you we are completely unbiased about their religious or cultural source\'97all worthy prophesies are equal in our eyes. As one, shall we say,
\f3\i  
\f1\i0 approaches fulmination, we initiate certain astute and\'97must I stress?\'97completely systemic and minimal interventions to assure their \'85\'92 Kleoboulos waved his arms portentously.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Fulmination?\'92 Sarah tested sceptically.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos almost nodded his hoody off. \'91Yes! Yes! You follow!\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Barely.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos beheld the Gyges Disc at Sarah\'92s fingertips and almost failed to prevent his eyes ejecting from their sockets. He nodded at it for his colleagues to notice. They fell into a state of awe.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny recovered enough to claim his man-sized share of the conversation, which is to say, all of it, but Sarah waved him down. Implicitly, he knew compliance was the better faring around Sarah so, with much restraint, he contained delivering his piece of mind to the lunatic.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91So, prophecy facilitation is busy concern, is it?\'92 Sarah continued.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos folded his hands solemnly and shifted on his feet. \'91It\'92s been a quiet few decades\'97generations, to be truthful. But, we have a side project!\'92 His eyes glowed and he had the face of a bearded Jack-O-Lantern.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91A side project,\'92 Sarah was expert at lacing words with disinterest, and she effortlessly deployed her expertise.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yes! Yes! Time is of the essence. Winter is coming! By which I mean, Christmas.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah\'92s eyes rolled. \'91We\'92re in the southern hemisphere.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Are we?\'92 Kleoboulos looked about and, for the first time, seemed aware of how he was dressed. \'91I\'92m sorry, I must be suffering Travelator lag.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Oh, tax my gambling! \'91Your offices are on the Travelator?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91They are, but let me assure you, we occupy a trio of the more functional cars. And, to be truthful, in a business like ours, the Travelator\'92s unpredictability and inaccessibility far exceeds what we could possibly hope for in any other office park. Although \'85\'92 Kleoboulos examined his pyjamas. \'91We must have been in bed when the Travelator arrived at the station. That old thing moves so slow, you never know where you are, mostly because you can\'92t believe you\'92re still in the same place as when you got on \'85\'92 He appeared to lose his train of thought.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We are the three sages of the Travelator,\'92 Solo, one of Kleoboulos\'92s attendants, said and nodded like a muppet, possibly Fozzy Bear.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As a side note, 
\f3\i The Muppet Show
\f1\i0  is one of the few phenomena to exist across all known universes in which conscious awareness has evolved, eclipsing even Elvis Presley who exists in 97.68%. Curiously, Fozzy Bear is the only muppet to exist across all Muppet Shows. Kermit the Frog exists in barely 60% of them, while Miss Piggy is a statistical anomaly, extant only in universes where the forces of good actually believe they have a chance against the forces of evil. Currently, guerrilla Miss Piggies are banding together across these universes, with the sole purpose of taking over the whole dang show. 
\f3\i Hiya.
\f1\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sorry, what?\'92 Sarah asked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We are the threes sages of the Travelator,\'92 Solo repeated.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah checked Kleoboulos\'92s business card. \'91Aren\'92t there seven sages?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos shrugged. \'91Ah, yes, well. We had artistic differences, you see.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah winced a thin smile. She didn\'92t see.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The others are on hiatus,\'92 the third sage, Chilo, said. \'91To pursue personal projects.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91They\'92ll be back,\'92 said Solo.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny found a moment to cut through. \'91So you\'92re looking for a hero?\'92 he asked hopefully.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Indeed we are, young Stoat,\'92 Kleoboulos said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny smoothed down his jacket as self-satisfaction broke out in a rash across his face.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos addressed Sarah. \'91We have a sacred mission to ask of you,\'92 he said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny\'92s happiness fizzled.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Me?\'92 Sarah felt a trap closing around her. \'91Why me?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Because you\'92re perfect,\'92 said Solo.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You\'92re invincible,\'92 said Chilo.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The word sliced through Sarah\'92s heart. They knew her! She was exposed. \'91What is it you want of me?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos stood stiff with formality. He knew everything depended on this. \'91We\'92d rather like to know, if it isn\'92t too much trouble, that is. Sarah. Could we get you pregnant?\'92\

